+# Disposable fancy-regex evidence spike
+
+Do not merge this branch. No engine/default/feature-loss decision is made here.
+
+Base: `4c02ffc8e116dc8bfbd3ba14592220a3f1a1a5ac`.
+The main worktree's `docs/wayfinder/issues/09-spike-fancy-regex.md` is the context pointer; its final report is `docs/wayfinder/assets/fancy-regex-spike.md` in that worktree.
+
+- `rust/src/regex.rs`: safe userdata-backed compiled tables, native matching/iteration/substitution, no pattern rewriting or PCRE2 fallback.
+- `rust/src/spike_replacement.rs`: finite replacement grammar with eight unit tests; not exhaustive PCRE2 compatibility.
+- `data/core/regex.lua`: preserves nil holes in approved capture returns.
+- `rust/examples/fancy_engine_probe.rs`: raw engine Unicode/flag probes.
+- `spike/`: frozen Lua corpus, baseline runtime and additional probes used for this assessment.
+- `fancy-api-notes.md`: pinned primary API references plus corrections from host observations.
+
+Experiment settings only: 1,000,000 backtracks per native capture execution, plus a separate 1,000,000-match-call quota per composed operation; 8 MiB substitution output. These are not agreed product defaults and do not prove a unified work budget. `regex.set_limits(work,output)` is spike-only configuration; its protocol is not selected for shipping.
+
+Build/test/stage from this worktree:
+
+```sh
+nix develop --command bash -c 'cargo build --release --manifest-path rust/Cargo.toml && cargo test --release --manifest-path rust/Cargo.toml spike_replacement:: && LITE_RELEASE=1 scripts/install-linux.sh rust/target/release/lite-xl rust/target/stage /usr/local >/dev/null'
+```
+
+Copy `spike/*.lua` into a disposable `LITE_USERDIR`. Run with SDL_VIDEODRIVER=dummy, DBUS_SESSION_BUS_ADDRESS=unix:path=/nonexistent/lxl-contract-bus, SDL_FILE_DIALOG_DRIVER empty, LITE_OS_HOME at that directory and LITE_PREFIX at this worktree's rust/target/stage/usr/local. Use `prlimit --core=0:0 --as=2147483648 --cpu=20:25 -- timeout -k 2 30` around the release binary.
+
+- Corpus: `LITE_XL_RUNTIME=regex-acceptance REGEX_CORPUS_MODE=candidate` (expected five incompatibility failures).
+- Additional checks: `LITE_XL_RUNTIME=fancy-regex-probe FANCY_CASE=dialect|safety|limits` (dialect fails; candidate-only safety/limits checks pass). Never execute candidate-only unsafe-reference scenarios on the original raw-pointer implementation.
+- Workloads: `LITE_XL_RUNTIME=regex-release-baseline BASELINE_CASE=<case> BASELINE_ROOT=<public reference checkout> BASELINE_DIR=<disposable userdir>`; cases and dimensions are in the runtime header. Five JavaScript cases are blocked, not benchmark passes.
+
+Successful limited examples or fast medians are not evidence of engine adoption readiness. See the main-worktree report for exact failing patterns, matched reference measurements, unsupported inputs and unresolved limits.
