+# fancy-regex 0.19.2 API notes (advisory, spike only)
+
+Pinned sources: docs.rs 0.19.2 + tag `0.19.2` source (commit e268485).
+No engine decision implied. Host probes are authoritative for the evaluated adapter: with input assertion overrides disabled, even `^`/`$` suppression was ineffective; enabling them made the protected NOTBOL case pass but also suppressed absolute `\\A`/`\\z`, unlike PCRE2. This mapping remains a documented adapter gap.
+
+## Verified signatures (0.19.2)
+
+- `RegexBuilder::new(pat: &str) -> Self` + `case_insensitive/multi_line/ignore_whitespace/dot_matches_new_line/verbose_mode/unicode_mode/oniguruma_mode/crlf/bytes_mode/backtrack_limit/delegate_size_limit/delegate_dfa_size_limit/find_not_empty/seek(+_filter)/allow_input_assertion_overrides -> &mut Self` + `build() -> Result<Regex>`. ([builder](https://docs.rs/fancy-regex/0.19.2/fancy_regex/struct.RegexBuilder.html))
+- `unicode_mode(false)`: `\w\d\s`→ASCII-only on `&str`; `\W\D\S`, bare `.`, `\p{...}` **fail to compile** on `&str`; use `BytesMode::Ascii` + `&[u8]` for byte semantics. Inline `(?u)/(?-u)` must match builder or `ParseError::ChangingUnicodeModeUnsupported`. ([options](https://docs.rs/fancy-regex/0.19.2/fancy_regex/struct.RegexOptionsBuilder.html))
+- `RegexInput::new(h)`, `.from_pos(u)`, `.range(R)` (panics if out of bounds), `.anchored(bool)` (match only at exact start), `.start_text(bool)` (`^`/`\A`), `.end_text(bool)` (`$`/`\z`), `.continue_from_previous_match_end(bool)` (`\G`) — **suppression-only**: `false`=suppress, `true`=clear override. Full haystack kept for anchors/lookaround; offsets absolute. ([input](https://docs.rs/fancy-regex/0.19.2/fancy_regex/struct.RegexInput.html)) ([source](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/fancy-regex/fancy-regex/0.19.2/src/input.rs))
+- `\A`/`\z` suppression additionally requires `allow_input_assertion_overrides(true)` (default off); runtime overrides otherwise ignored. ([options](https://docs.rs/fancy-regex/0.19.2/fancy_regex/struct.RegexOptionsBuilder.html))
+- `Regex::{new, find/find_input/find_from_pos, captures/captures_input/captures_from_pos, is_match/is_match_input, find_iter(_input), captures_iter(_input), captures_len, capture_names, replace}`. ([regex](https://docs.rs/fancy-regex/0.19.2/fancy_regex/struct.Regex.html))
+- `Captures::get(i) -> Option<Match>` (`0`=whole), `Captures::name(n)`. ([captures](https://docs.rs/fancy-regex/0.19.2/fancy_regex/struct.Captures.html))
+- `find_not_empty(true)` + always-empty pattern → `CompileError::PatternCanNeverMatch` at build. ([options](https://docs.rs/fancy-regex/0.19.2/fancy_regex/struct.RegexOptionsBuilder.html)) ([variants](https://docs.rs/fancy-regex/0.19.2/fancy_regex/enum.CompileError.html))
+- `backtrack_limit(n)` default 1M; exceed → `Error::RuntimeError(BacktrackLimitExceeded)`. ([options](https://docs.rs/fancy-regex/0.19.2/fancy_regex/struct.RegexOptionsBuilder.html)) ([runtime](https://docs.rs/fancy-regex/0.19.2/fancy_regex/enum.RuntimeError.html))
+- `delegate_size_limit / delegate_dfa_size_limit` forwarded to `regex` crate; effective bound ≈ `n_delegated × limit`. ([options](https://docs.rs/fancy-regex/0.19.2/fancy_regex/struct.RegexOptionsBuilder.html))
+- Lookbehind: fixed-width always; variable needs `variable-lookbehinds` (default on) else `LookBehindNotConst`/`VariableLookBehindRequiresFeature`; backrefs inside variable lookbehind unsupported (reverse-DFA path). ([compile-errors](https://docs.rs/fancy-regex/0.19.2/fancy_regex/enum.CompileError.html)) ([syntax](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/fancy-regex/fancy-regex/0.19.2/docs/syntax.md))
+- Verbs: only `(*FAIL)` documented; **no `(*MARK)`/`(*SKIP)` etc.** ([syntax](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/fancy-regex/fancy-regex/0.19.2/docs/syntax.md))
+
+## Spike recommendations
+
+- Flags: `case_insensitive(true)`/`multi_line(true)`/`dot_matches_new_line(true)` are leads to test. **Correction from host probes:** `unicode_mode(false)` or ASCII byte matching is NOT a demonstrated PCRE UTF+UCP-off solution: the former rejects UTF-8-capable `.`/negated classes and loses non-ASCII case folding; generic byte matching can split UTF-8. No such workaround was adopted.
+- ANCHORED→`RegexInput::anchored(true)`; NOTBOL-ish→`.start_text(false)`; NOTEOL-ish→`.end_text(false)`; also test `allow_input_assertion_overrides(true)` for `\A\z`.
+- Empty-match: spike `find_not_empty(true)` on `a*` (expect build error) vs `a*|b` (mixed-alternative same-position retry — behavior unverified, test empirically).
+- Budget: set small `backtrack_limit` + small `delegate_*_limits`; treat `BacktrackLimitExceeded` as work exhaustion, NOT a deadline/timeout guarantee.
+
+## Hard blockers / gaps (must spike, not assume)
+
+1. No cancellation handle / deadline / aggregate operation budget in 0.19.2 API — only per-regex `backtrack_limit` + delegate size caps. Long scans need outer timeout.
+2. `backtrack_limit` reset scope (per `find` call vs per iterator step) is undocumented — measure with `captures_iter` over many matches.
+3. No NOTBOL/NOTEOL/ANCHORED names; suppression-only `start_text/end_text(true)`=no-op differs from PCRE — verify each mapping empirically.
+4. `(*MARK)` unsupported (only `(*FAIL)`); unicode-case edge behavior delegates to `regex` crate — verify, don't assume.
+5. Local 0.19.2 crate-cache path not confirmed from here (no shell); canonical pinned sources above + tag `0.19.2` (e268485). Report actual registry path from the spike host.
